! Transient (dynamic) simulation with the small-strain J2 plasticity UMAT
! "plastic" of UMATLib (additive split, von Mises yield, isotropic hardening,
! radial return with the consistent tangent): vibration of a cantilever beam
! under a suddenly applied body force, Bossak method.
!
! The hardening curve (Material Constants: nu, then uniaxial total strain /
! stress points) gives E = 70 GPa, yield at 2 MPa and linear hardening to
! 4 MPa at 2e-4 total strain, perfectly plastic after that. The peak bending
! stress is a few MPa, so the root of the beam yields: the maximum equivalent
! plastic strain (state variable 8, column 3 of SaveScalars) reaches 7.3e-5,
! and the tip deflection at t = 0.02 (the reference norm) is about 57 % larger
! than the elastic one (2.767e-4). The finite-strain model "fplastic" on the
! same case (test UMAT_fplastic_transient) agrees with this to 2e-5.

Header
  CHECK KEYWORDS Warn
  Mesh DB "." "beam"
End
Simulation
  Max Output Level = 4
  Coordinate System = Cartesian 2D
  Simulation Type = Transient
  Timestepping Method = Bossak
  Timestep Intervals = 40
  Timestep Sizes = 5.0e-4
  Output Intervals = 0
  Steady State Max Iterations = 1
End

Body 1
  Equation = 1
  Material = 1
  Body Force = 1
End
Body Force 1
  Stress Bodyforce 2 = -1.0e5
End
Material 1
  Number of Material Constants = Integer 5
  Number of State Variables = Integer 8
Material Constants(5) = Real 0.3 2.857142857E-5 2.0E6 2.0E-4 4.0E6
  UMAT Subroutine = File "UMATLib" "plastic"
  Name = "plastic"
  Density = 2700.0
  Reference Temperature = 293.0
End
Solver 1
  Equation = Elasticity Solver
  Variable = Displacement
  Variable DOFs = 2
  Procedure = "ElasticSolve" "ElasticSolver"
  Linear System Solver = Direct
  Nonlinear System Max Iterations = 10
  Nonlinear System Convergence Tolerance = 1.0e-9
  Large Deflection = False

End
Solver 2
  Exec Solver = After Timestep
  Equation = SaveScalars
  Procedure = "SaveData" "SaveScalars"
  Filename = f.dat
  Variable 1 = Time
  Variable 2 = Displacement 2
  Operator 2 = min
  Variable 3 = UmatState 8
  Operator 3 = max
  Show Norm Index = 2
End
Equation 1
  Active Solvers(2) = 1 2
  Plane Stress = False
End
Boundary Condition 1
  Target Boundaries = 1
  Displacement 1 = 0
  Displacement 2 = 0
End

! = |min vertical displacement| at t = 0.02 (elastic: 2.767e-4)
Solver 2 :: Reference Norm = Real 4.35908617E-04
Solver 2 :: Reference Norm Tolerance = Real 1.0e-7
